From 00c0bdae7cfbfb76e32d0073af1fe1ce07b4dbe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:08:03 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] kcm_kwindecoration: gallery first, buttons and border
 size on one sub-page, previews off the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Gallery (docs/page-design.md section 1). Config keys, kcfg, KDecoration plugins, KNS and the reload
D-Bus signal are unchanged.

Moved / renamed (inventory/relabel/kcm_kwindecoration.tsv):
- Toolbar now holds only "Buttons and Borders…" (was "Configure Titlebar Buttons…") and "Get New…".
- "Window border size:" moved from the toolbar to the top of that sub-page, now "Titlebar Buttons and Borders"
  (kcm_kwindecoration/borderSize, configure-titlebar). The combo is the same control with the same highlighter.
- ksr: markers on the changed and text-only rows (edit-theme, buttons-hint, get-new).

Speed (cause from code, not measured):
- Every grid cell built a KDecoration Bridge + Settings + two live Decoration previews synchronously inside
  its delegate (Themes.qml, old lines 40-60). They now live in a Component behind a Loader { asynchronous: true },
  so the grid, labels and toolbar are shown first and the previews fill in cell by cell.
- The per-theme "Edit … Theme…" bridge is created only when that action is used (it shared the preview bridge before).
- Not changed: DecorationsModel::init() still does findPlugins + instantiatePlugin (dlopen) on the UI thread, one
  queued event-loop turn after construction (decorationmodel.cpp:115-130); moving it needs a build to test.
- Numbers: before ~1.7 s under load (ranking only). After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-019, HIG-057.

Not built yet (freeze). Unconfirmed: async Loader around KDecoration.Decoration items (previews were created with
anchors.fill: parent; the Loader item is the parent now) and creating KDecoration.Bridge through Component.createObject.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
